{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What Types of Requirements Do You Know?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to discuss types of requirements."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Interpret the requirements report to determine the technological needs in managing information, based on rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Participates in simple conversations or simulated situations about the communicative topics for this level through grammar and vocabulary structures.  Recognizes simple ideas on requirement reports, tools for Object Oriented Programming, and other basic programming tools."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Simple and Present Continuous in Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <span class=\"strong\">present simple tense</span> to talk about permanent situations such as habits or general facts.  On the other hand, we use the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span> when we talk about temporary facts in the present; things that are happening at the moment. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm not going out tonight, I have to bring this work forward."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You aren't doing very well, you have a bunch of requirement types over there."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't intent to narrow down the requirements into small groups."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't have time to talk over this now."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are some of the most common uses of the <span class=\"strong\">present simple</span>  and the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>:<br /><br />  <span class=\"strong\">Present Simple</span><br /> To talk about permanent situations:<br /> <br /> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">work</span> in a software company. </span><br /><br /> To talk about routines or habits:<br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">A software developer always <span class=\"strong\">needs</span> to check the users' needs.</span><br /><br /> To talk about general truth:<br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">Every software package <span class=\"strong\">has</span> to meet different requirements. </span> <br /><br />  When we need to make negative statements in the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>, we need to add the auxiliary verbs <span class=\"strong\">do</span> or <span class=\"strong\">does</span> plus the particle <span class=\"strong\">not</span> or we can use the contracted forms <span class=\"strong\">don't</span> or <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> : <br /><br />  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">don't/doesn't</span> + <span class=\"strong\">verb in base form</span> + complement. </div><br /><br />   Remember that we use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">does/doesn't</span> for the third person singular (he, she, it) and <span class=\"strong\">do/don't</span> for the other personal pronouns. <br /><br />  Examples:<br />  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">don't work</span> in a software company.<br /> A software developer <span class=\"strong\">doesn't need</span> to check the user's needs. <br /> Every software package <span class=\"strong\">doesn't have</span>  to meet different requirements. </span><br /><br />  Notice that when we use the auxiliary verbs <span class=\"strong\">don't</span> or <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span>, the main verb keeps its base form. In the examples above, the verbs <span class=\"strong\">work, need</span> or <span class=\"strong\">have</span> do not change. <br /><br />  <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span><br /><br /> To describe an action in progress:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">I<span class=\"strong\"> 'm checking </span>the software settings.</span><br /><br />  To describe a temporary situation: <br />  <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">is doing</span> a software requirement study at the moment.</span><br /><br />   When we make negative statements in the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span>, we just have to add the negative word <span class=\"strong\">not</span> next to the verb to <span class=\"strong\">be</span>. You can also use the contracted forms <span class=\"strong\">isn't</span> and <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span>; but remember that for the first person singular, there is not contraction of <span class=\"strong\">not</span>:  <br /><br />  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">am not/is not/are not</span>+ <span class=\"strong\">verb in ING</span> + complement.</div><br /><br />   Examples:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">I<span class=\"strong\">'m\u00a0not\u00a0checking</span> the software requirements. <br />She <span class=\"strong\">is not checking</span> the software requirements at the moment. \u00a0<br />You <span class=\"strong\">aren't recording</span> the interviews. </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs to Solve Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Phrasal verbs</span> combine a verb with a preposition or adverb. When these works are together, they have a completely different meaning from the one they have when they are separated. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't intent to narrow down the requirements into small groups."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I just need to sort out how to organize the functional, architectural, structural, and behavioral requirements."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sweetie, I don't have time to talk over this now, I need to get this done."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Those are statements of fact and assumptions that see about expectations of a system. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " For instance, when you have the verb <span class=\"strong\">get</span>, in the following sentence:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">gets</span> some good material to understand the software requirements.</span> <br /><br />  This verb has the meaning of collecting or obtaining something, but in the case of:<br /><br />  <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">got through</span> her work. </span><br /><br />  The phrasal verb <span class=\"strong\">get through</span> makes reference to finishing something.  <br /><br />  In the following chart, we have a list of <span class=\"strong\">phrasal verbs</span> that may be useful when you need to talk about <span class=\"strong\">solving problems</span>: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Phrasal verbs</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Examples</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Deal with </span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To manage a situation. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We have to deal with the errors the software may have.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Narrow (sth) down </span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" To reduce something.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We need to narrow the list of software errors down. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sort out <br /> Sort (sth) out </span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" To find a solution for a situation.  <br /><br /> To organize. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">They have to sort out the computer program's initial problems. <br /> I'm sorting my ideas out. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">See about </span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" To examine something or to prepare something. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">You should see about doing another software requirement study. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Talk  (sth) over  </span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" To discuss, to debate \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">We should talk it over with the project manager.  </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bunch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You have a bunch of requirement types over there.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suitability  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the fact of being appropriated for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Customer requirements help us estimate the system's suitability and effectiveness. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "encompass "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cover or include a set of elements"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Requirements encompass needs and statements of different kinds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "top-level "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the most important aspects of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Functional requirements are used as the top-level functions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "constraint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a restriction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Those expectations are mission, objectives, environment, and constraints. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n3le01ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read more information about types of requirements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a mind map about different types of requirements."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use different colors and write details."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Expose the information to your instructor and classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I review the lesson or look for more information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I summarize the information to create my mind map."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use color to link ideas and details."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my work to my instructor and classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can identify different types of requirements."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can understand why there are different types of requirements."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can ask questions related to different types of requirements."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How would you define software engineering?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What aspects does a software developer need to define before creating a computer program?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Every new project has to meet certain specifications.  "}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " What do requirements